From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: orangepi_zero2: drop the RNDIS Ethernet gadget

CONFIG_USB_ETHER defaults to y on sunxi with the MUSB gadget. It
registers a fake "usb_ether" network device at boot which only ever prints

  Allwinner mUSB OTG (Peripheral)
  Net:   eth0: ethernet@5020000using musb-hdrc, OUT ep1out IN ep1in STATUS ep2in
  MAC de:ad:be:ef:00:01
  HOST MAC de:ad:be:ef:00:00
  RNDIS ready
  , eth1: usb_ether

on the Zero2, whose USB-C port is power/peripheral only and never used
for RNDIS networking. The MUSB gadget itself (fastboot, ums) is kept.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -28,3 +28,4 @@
 CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
+# CONFIG_USB_ETHER is not set
